  "description": "TPO 53/1984 T157 Hornbeam T158 horse chestnut.\r\nT1: Horse chestnut: Previously pollarded. This tree has a significant cavity on the east side of the main trunk with extensive decay extending into the upper crown. The tree is heavily biased weighted towards the road and footway (west side) and the cavity is located in the central crown break union. The tree is approximately 12m high. We would recommend that the tree is reduced approximately 3m below the previous pollard points to reduce the weight and stress leading on the central crown break creating a framework for future growth with the aim to retain the tree in a safe condition as long as possible leaving a final finished height of approximately 9m. T2: Hornbeam: Pollard to previous points (approximately 2m). To continue cyclical maintenance cycle and maintain the tree within its surroundings and minimum 2.5m clearance to buildings.",
